  "notes": "{倒|たお}す means to knock down or defeat. A transitive godan verb.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- {倒|たお}す ({他動詞|たどうし}): to knock down\n- {倒|たお}れる ({自動詞|じどうし}): to fall down, to collapse\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {敵|てき}を{倒|たお}す: to defeat the enemy\n- {木|き}を{倒|たお}す: to fell a tree\n- {花瓶|かびん}を{倒|たお}す: to knock over a vase\n- {政権|せいけん}を{倒|たお}す: to overthrow a regime\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{倒|たお}している typically means \"is lying down\" (result state) rather than \"is knocking down.\"",
